  "label": "woman's body mapped as 'dishwasher ready for another load'",
  "description": "The text 'when your dishwasher is ready for another load' is an analogical mapping that projects the woman's physical body (specifically her bare legs and underwear, emphasized in the visual) onto the metaphorical concept of a dishwasher being 'ready'. This mapping relies on the double entendre: the literal function of a dishwasher (needs dishes to be loaded) is humorously equated with the woman's body being 'ready' for another load — a play on sexual availability. The visual of the woman in minimal clothing is framed to be the punchline, creating a humorous or suggestive tone rooted in objectification and misogynous stereotypes.",
